diff --git a/docs/src/platform-support.md b/docs/src/platform-support.md
index b90f1f1..7e66301 100644
--- a/docs/src/platform-support.md
+++ b/docs/src/platform-support.md
@@ -62,5 +62,19 @@ host's pointer width, but does not establish that an address is valid to access.
-This initial target support only establishes Rust layout and integer behavior.
-Integer-pointer casts remain rejected, and selecting this target does not yet
-enable physical memory operations or change logical storage classes. Physical
-addressing, alignment and alias rules require separate lowering and validation.
-The layout compiletests do not execute shaders or dereference synthetic values.
+The target requires SPIR-V 1.3 or later and emits PhysicalStorageBuffer64 with
+PhysicalStorageBufferAddresses and Int64. The physical-storage extension is
+declared when targeting SPIR-V before 1.5. Only PhysicalStorageBuffer pointers
+represent integer addresses. Ordinary logical storage classes keep their
+meaning, and converting a logical pointer to an integer is diagnosed.
+
+Integer/raw-pointer casts support 64-bit address transport across function
+boundaries. Narrow integer casts convert the address to 64 bits before normal
+truncation. Integer-to-pointer casts extend according to the source integer's
+signedness, following Rust's cast rules. Existing targets still reject raw
+address conversions. Function parameters and pointer slots receive conservative
+Aliased/AliasedPointer decorations when required, preserving an existing
+explicit restriction rather than inventing a no-alias guarantee.
+
+This experimental support does not yet provide a physical-memory access API.
+Aligned loads/stores, pointer arithmetic and comparisons, aggregate pointer
+storage, atomics and reference validity need separate lowering and evidence.
+Do not infer those guarantees from a valid conversion. The source compiletests
+transport synthetic values without dereferencing them and do not execute shaders.
